n Trump pulled $400 million worth of funding. That's the lifeblood is the federal money for these universities, $400 million. Well, what happened? Columbia University, just today, very quickly expelled. some of the students who had taken over Halton Hall during last year's protests. They've expelled or suspended the students and they've revoked the diplomas of some of the students, even some who've graduated. How about that? How about that letter in the mail? The university said its judicial board had issued its sanctions against dozens of students who had occupied Hamilton Hall based on the severity of their behaviors. No breakdown was cited. And as I said, Mahmoud Khalil, who organized it, is in a federal jail right now. And Trump is saying that's the first of many arrests. We're simply like, enough is enough. We're not putting up with this crap anymore. And I hope this spirit enters California because there's so much nonsense going on here that we just shouldn't put up with anymore. No more debate, no more seeing both sides, trying to convince, no, just save your energy, just out, out, out, out. And it's amazing how withdrawing $400 million worth of funding is going to do. This went on in April of 2024. And they're all going to finally get justice. You see how quickly that changes things? You decide to enforce the law, you decide to take action, you decide to be tough about it, not cowed by demonstrators or people trying to emotionally manipulate you or shame you, just saying enough of your garbage out. Get the F out.",
